## 3.2 Student document extraction

The backend must extract:

- USN.
- Student Name.
- DOB.

The system must identify actual student table headings and correctly associate every field with its value.

Do not simply read consecutive text lines and assume three consecutive values form a student row.

Support:

- Different table layouts.
- Multiple-page tables.
- Different column widths.
- Different fonts.
- Different DOB formats.
- Text-based PDFs.
- Scanned PDFs.
- Image-based student lists.

## 3.3 Department, semester and section context

The Department must come from the authenticated HOD account.

The Semester must come from the Setup Class semester selector.

The Section must come from the selected Student Lists section tab.

If the uploaded document contains department, semester or section information, extract it as document-level metadata.

Do NOT insert document metadata into student rows.

Example document header:

Department: CSE  
Semester: 5  
Section: B

The standard Excel student table must contain only:

| USN | Student Name | DOB |
|---|---|---|
| 4MH24CS071 | Aarav Deshmukh | 2006-03-12 |
| 4MH24CS072 | Bhavana Krishnamurthy | 2006-06-19 |

These are illustrative records only.

Compare extracted document metadata against:

- Authenticated HOD department.
- Selected semester.
- Selected section.

If metadata conflicts with the selected context, block the conversion from being marked valid and display a clear context mismatch.

If section metadata is unavailable, retain the selected section context and require appropriate HOD confirmation according to the existing workflow.

If a document contains student records belonging to different sections, do not silently merge them into the selected section. Identify those records and require the HOD to resolve the mismatch.

Do not add Department, Semester or Section columns to the standard student Excel template unless the approved institutional template is deliberately revised.

